WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.700
We spent this series on the server side of a call.

2
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.980
But every service is also a client.

3
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.340
Chenile treats the outbound side with the same respect:

4
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:16.090
no hand-written transport, and interception on the way out.

5
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.290
Chenile ships its own service registry:

6
00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:23.130
remote services, their operations, and every parameter.

7
00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:24.950
It's database-backed, cached,

8
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:27.200
and fingerprinted for change detection

9
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.160
— and it's the same registry that

10
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.310
carries each service's policies.

11
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.500
To call another service, ask for a proxy of its interface.

12
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.650
The object you get back implements that interface.

13
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:40.300
Call it like a local object

14
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.860
— and a header copier carries correlation,

15
00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.700
identity and tenant along.

16
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:48.000
A router decides where the call goes.

17
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:48.640
Same JVM?

18
00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.430
A direct, in-process call

19
00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:52.320
— that's your modulith.

20
00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:53.460
Somewhere else?

21
00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.050
A remote call over HTTP

22
00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.380
— or an event through pub-sub.

23
00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:59.300
Deploy the callee separately,

24
00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.920
and the identical caller code goes remote.

25
00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.300
You changed deployment

26
00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.240
— not code.

27
00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:05.850
Now the payoff.

28
00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:09.070
On the way out, the proxy runs a client-side chain

29
00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:11.820
— Chenile calls them client processors.

30
00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:14.350
Header propagation, the auth token,

31
00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:17.050
correlation, logging, retry and timeout

32
00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:19.200
— then a response handler turns

33
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.810
the reply back into typed objects.

34
00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:25.990
And the chain is configurable per service, and per operation.

35
00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:29.540
Add a retry to one operation, a header to one service

36
00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:31.060
— by configuration.

37
00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:33.030
Server pipeline in.

38
00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.920
Client-processor chain out.

39
00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.800
One interception philosophy

40
00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:38.510
— in both directions.

41
00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:39.480
Next:

42
00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:40.180
the finale.

43
00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:43.310
A tour of a governed system, from end to end.
